{{also|hésitant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|haesitans}}, present participle of {{m|la|haesito|haesitare|to stick fast, to hesitate}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Tending to [[hesitate]], [[wait]], or proceed with [[caution]] or [[reservation]].
#: ''I am '''hesitant''' to recommend him as a manager because he has a short temper.''

